        "text": "PRE-ADMISSION TESTING VISIT\nVisit date: 02/26/2026\nPlanned procedure: carpal tunnel release\n\nVITAL SIGNS: See flowsheet.\n\nMEDICATION RECONCILIATION (patient-reported):\n  - tamsulosin 0.4 mg PO nightly - taking as prescribed\n  - atorvastatin 40 mg PO nightly - taking as prescribed\n  - Patient also reports taking Xarelto 20 mg (daily with evening meal), prescribed by an outside cardiologist; not on the reconciled medication list - flagged for provider review.\n\nALLERGIES reviewed and confirmed. Denies fever, chills, cough, or recent illness.\n\nPAIN: 4/10 at lower back, managed with acetaminophen.\nSKIN: intact; no rashes, open wounds, or pressure injuries at the planned surgical site.\nFUNCTIONAL STATUS: independent with ADLs.\nPRIOR ANESTHESIA: uncomplicated general anesthesia in the past.\nADVANCE DIRECTIVE: patient declines to complete at this time. Health care proxy: sibling.\nPSYCHOSOCIAL: reports mild anxiety about surgery; coping strategies discussed.\n\nNPO instructions: nothing to eat after midnight; clear liquids until 2 hours before arrival. Patient verbalized understanding.\nFall risk: moderate. Ride home arranged with friend.\nEducation provided on incentive spirometry, pain management expectations, and chlorhexidine skin prep."
