        "text": "PREOPERATIVE HISTORY AND PHYSICAL\nDate of service: 02/21/2026\nPatient: Grace Lopez    DOB: 01/01/1941\nPlanned procedure: carpal tunnel release (scheduled for 03/01/2026)\n\nCHIEF COMPLAINT: Numbness and tingling of the left hand.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS: 85-year-old female referred by Hand Surgery for pre-operative evaluation prior to carpal tunnel release. EMG/NCS confirmed moderate-to-severe median neuropathy at the wrist; nocturnal symptoms have not improved with splinting. Patient denies recent illness, hospitalizations, or changes in medications over the past month. Functional capacity estimated at approximately 4 METs (walks one block briskly).\n\nPAST MEDICAL HISTORY: Atrial fibrillation.\nPAST SURGICAL HISTORY: None.\n\nMEDICATIONS:\n  - tamsulosin 0.4 mg PO nightly\n  - atorvastatin 40 mg PO nightly\nALLERGIES: Codeine (nausea)\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY: Never smoker. Retired teacher.\nFAMILY HISTORY: Mother with breast cancer.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS: Negative for dysuria, night sweats, easy bruising, cough, melena, hematochezia, chills. All other systems reviewed and negative.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM:\n  Vitals 10:05  BP 127/74, HR 68, T 98.0 F, SpO2 97% RA\n  General: Alert, oriented, no acute distress.\n  Airway: Mallampati II, full neck range of motion.\n  CV: Irregularly irregular rhythm, rate controlled, no murmurs.\n  Lungs: Clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n  Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended.\n  Extremities: No edema.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN:\n  85-year-old female being evaluated prior to carpal tunnel release. Cardiac risk acceptable for planned surgery.\n  1. Carpal tunnel release scheduled for 03/01/2026 with Hand Surgery.\n  2. Pre-operative labs per protocol; results to be reviewed prior to surgery.\n  3. Continue home medications except as directed by perioperative instructions.\n  4. Risks and benefits of surgery discussed at a high level; formal consent per surgical team.\n\nElectronically signed by Brian O'Connor on 02/21/2026."
